  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08A5">Corollary <span data-tag="08A5">3.2.1.5</span>.</a>unstraightening functorUnphi+@$Un^{+}_{\phi }$ Let $S$ be a simplicial set, $\calC $ a simplicial category, and $\phi : \sCoNerve [S] \rightarrow \calC ^{op}$ any simplicial functor. The straightening functor $St^{+}_{\phi }$ has a right adjoint </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[ Un^{+}_{\phi }: (\mSet )^{\calC } \rightarrow (\mSet )_{/S}. \]
</div>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from part $(1)$ of Proposition <a href="/tag/11FA" data-tag="11FA">3.2.1.4</a> and the adjoint functor theorem. (Alternatively, one can construct $Un^{+}_{\phi }$ directly; we leave details to the reader.) 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
